1
00:00:01,835 --> 00:00:03,070
EPISODE 18

2
00:00:03,136 --> 00:00:05,072
Who are you? You can't be in here.

3
00:00:05,138 --> 00:00:07,908
-Please leave.
-Step outside.

4
00:00:11,011 --> 00:00:13,113
Are you Lee Hyeon-seok?

5
00:00:14,047 --> 00:00:15,616
And you are?

6
00:00:19,119 --> 00:00:21,088
-Ugh!
-Hyeon-seok!

7
00:00:21,154 --> 00:00:22,756
Are you okay?

8
00:00:24,057 --> 00:00:27,060
What are you doing? Just who are you?

9
00:00:27,127 --> 00:00:30,097
Me? I'm like a brother to Yun-hui

10
00:00:30,163 --> 00:00:32,232
and Min-ho's uncle, you bastard!

11
00:00:32,299 --> 00:00:35,702
You bastard!
Let go, let go, let go! Ow, it hurts!

12
00:00:35,769 --> 00:00:37,371
-Let go of me!
-Get over here!

13
00:00:37,437 --> 00:00:38,972
-Hey!
-Are you even human?

14
00:00:39,039 --> 00:00:40,140
-Your hand!
-Let go!

15
00:00:41,141 --> 00:00:43,777
Boy, Ki-jun is such a jerk.

16
00:00:43,844 --> 00:00:45,979
No matter how things turned out,

17
00:00:46,046 --> 00:00:48,482
how could he leave without a goodbye?

18
00:00:48,549 --> 00:00:50,284
It must've been so hard on him.

19
00:00:50,350 --> 00:00:52,319
I just hope his feelings aren't hurt.

20
00:00:53,854 --> 00:00:54,988
Um, Yun-hui?

21
00:00:55,055 --> 00:00:58,659
That man earlier
was Min-ho's dad, right?

22
00:00:58,725 --> 00:01:00,160
What?

23
00:01:00,227 --> 00:01:02,596
Min-ho's dad? Did he come here again?

24
00:01:03,363 --> 00:01:05,732
-Yes.
-He did?

25
00:01:06,500 --> 00:01:09,369
Why would he come
all the way down here again?

26
00:01:09,436 --> 00:01:11,939
You're sure he didn't say much, right?

27
00:01:12,005 --> 00:01:14,374
Yes, I told you. He didn't say much.

28
00:01:14,441 --> 00:01:16,510
You don't need to worry about it.

29
00:01:20,180 --> 00:01:21,882
Yes, hello?

30
00:01:21,949 --> 00:01:23,984
Yes, speaking.

31
00:01:24,885 --> 00:01:26,620
What? What did you say?

32
00:01:27,454 --> 00:01:30,791
Yes, yes. I understand. Yes, okay.

33
00:01:31,792 --> 00:01:33,694
What was that call? Why so shocked?

34
00:01:33,760 --> 00:01:36,663
They say Min-gi's being held
at a Seoul police station.

35
00:01:36,730 --> 00:01:37,764
What?

36
00:01:37,831 --> 00:01:41,802
Why is Min-gi in Seoul?
A police station? Why was he taken in?

37
00:01:41,868 --> 00:01:45,305
The thing is, Min-gi, um…

38
00:01:45,372 --> 00:01:47,774
I think he fought with Min-ho's dad.

39
00:01:47,841 --> 00:01:51,011
What? They fought? Why?

40
00:01:51,078 --> 00:01:52,879
I don't know the details either.

41
00:01:52,946 --> 00:01:55,315
I think I should hurry to Seoul.

42
00:01:55,382 --> 00:01:58,318
-I'll go with you, Yun-hui.
-No, I'll go by myself.

43
00:01:58,385 --> 00:02:00,587
I think that's for the best right now.

44
00:02:06,693 --> 00:02:08,996
Hey, do you know anything?

45
00:02:09,062 --> 00:02:10,297
Huh?

46
00:02:11,365 --> 00:02:14,301
Uh, no, nothing.

47
00:02:23,310 --> 00:02:26,680
Oh, no, Min-gi! Min-gi!

48
00:02:26,747 --> 00:02:29,049
What on earth happened here?

49
00:02:29,616 --> 00:02:31,585
Why in the world did you do that?

50
00:02:31,652 --> 00:02:33,587
Please, just say something!

51
00:02:33,654 --> 00:02:35,088
Yun-hui.

52
00:02:45,932 --> 00:02:48,268
Anyway, I'm really sorry about this.

53
00:02:48,935 --> 00:02:50,337
It's okay.

54
00:02:50,404 --> 00:02:52,539
I didn't want to make a scene.

55
00:02:52,606 --> 00:02:55,509
My manager got so angry
that he reported it.

56
00:02:57,344 --> 00:02:59,513
-By the way, who is he?
-Huh?

57
00:03:00,380 --> 00:03:02,749
A younger guy from my neighborhood.

58
00:03:03,316 --> 00:03:04,818
I'm really sorry.

59
00:03:04,885 --> 00:03:07,688
And thank you so much
for letting this go quietly.

60
00:03:08,422 --> 00:03:11,425
-Really, it's fine.
-I'll get going then.

61
00:03:12,092 --> 00:03:13,493
Um, Yun-hui.

62
00:03:14,995 --> 00:03:17,798
Have you thought about what I said?

63
00:03:17,864 --> 00:03:20,934
I told you I don't need child support.

64
00:03:21,001 --> 00:03:23,870
Yun-hui, don't be like that.

65
00:03:23,937 --> 00:03:25,772
I don't need that lousy money.

66
00:03:25,839 --> 00:03:29,409
And I promised not to tell anyone
and to keep it a secret.

67
00:03:30,077 --> 00:03:32,012
But you know what?

68
00:03:32,979 --> 00:03:35,716
How can you not ask
a single thing about Min-ho?

69
00:03:36,516 --> 00:03:38,618
Even if you never wanted him,

70
00:03:38,685 --> 00:03:40,620
aren't you even curious about him?

71
00:03:40,687 --> 00:03:43,757
Don't you wonder how Min-ho
grew up without a dad,

72
00:03:43,824 --> 00:03:45,992
what he likes, if he's ever sick,

73
00:03:46,059 --> 00:03:47,294
or what he's like?

74
00:03:48,261 --> 00:03:50,130
Aren't you curious at all?

75
00:03:52,365 --> 00:03:54,267
He came to Seoul alone for his dad.

76
00:03:54,334 --> 00:03:56,236
Did you care if it shocked Min-ho,

77
00:03:56,303 --> 00:03:57,671
if he had a hard time,

78
00:03:57,738 --> 00:03:59,206
or if he cried?

79
00:04:00,974 --> 00:04:03,477
More than offering child support,

80
00:04:03,543 --> 00:04:07,347
more than asking me to keep a secret,
isn't that more important?

81
00:04:11,818 --> 00:04:13,587
I'll get going now.

82
00:04:14,521 --> 00:04:17,591
POLICE STATION

83
00:04:30,771 --> 00:04:34,074
What's wrong with you?
Why on earth did you do that?

84
00:04:34,141 --> 00:04:35,475
Why would you do that?

85
00:04:35,542 --> 00:04:37,511
How could I let a jerk like him go?

86
00:04:37,577 --> 00:04:41,414
What? He'll pay child support
if you keep quiet about Min-ho?

87
00:04:41,481 --> 00:04:45,652
That guy calls himself a dad?
What kind of father says that?

88
00:04:45,719 --> 00:04:48,588
-How do you know…
-I happened to overhear. So what?

89
00:04:48,655 --> 00:04:52,392
And how could you just stand there
after hearing garbage like that?

90
00:04:52,459 --> 00:04:53,894
It's about Min-ho and me.

91
00:04:53,960 --> 00:04:56,263
Who are you to care about us?

92
00:04:56,329 --> 00:04:59,132
And didn't I tell you
to stay out of our business?

93
00:04:59,199 --> 00:05:02,569
Fine, I was so sick and disgusted
that I tried not to care!

94
00:05:02,636 --> 00:05:04,771
But I can't help it if I keep caring!

95
00:05:04,838 --> 00:05:06,373
I don't want cheap pity.

96
00:05:06,439 --> 00:05:09,075
How many times do I have to tell you?

97
00:05:09,142 --> 00:05:12,813
Please just stop now,
because I can't take this anymore.

98
00:05:17,484 --> 00:05:19,119
That's not what it is.

99
00:05:24,291 --> 00:05:27,093
It's not sympathy, and it's not pity.

100
00:05:27,160 --> 00:05:28,528
Then what is it?

101
00:05:28,595 --> 00:05:31,131
I don't know… what this feeling is.

102
00:05:32,966 --> 00:05:36,570
But it's not like that.
I'm telling you, it's not like that.

103
00:05:54,254 --> 00:05:57,457
-Stop the car.
-Why all of a sudden?

104
00:05:58,925 --> 00:06:00,260
I'm hungry.

105
00:06:00,327 --> 00:06:02,662
-Buy me food.
-What?

106
00:06:03,363 --> 00:06:05,699
I haven't eaten a thing since morning.

107
00:06:22,716 --> 00:06:25,185
I'm sorry I made things hard for you.

108
00:06:25,252 --> 00:06:26,920
So you know you made it hard?

109
00:06:26,987 --> 00:06:28,788
I'm really sorry.

110
00:06:28,855 --> 00:06:30,223
Forget it.

111
00:06:30,290 --> 00:06:33,426
Thanks to you, I feel relieved too.

112
00:06:34,261 --> 00:06:37,697
Honestly, I regretted
not slapping him at least once myself.

113
00:06:37,764 --> 00:06:39,099
Really?

114
00:06:39,165 --> 00:06:41,268
That still doesn't mean you did well.

115
00:06:41,334 --> 00:06:43,937
A fistfight? You're not a kid, jeez.

116
00:06:47,908 --> 00:06:49,709
Eat slow, you'll get indigestion.

117
00:06:49,776 --> 00:06:52,345
I really thought I'd starve to death.

118
00:06:52,412 --> 00:06:55,415
I should've at least eaten
before coming to beat him up.

119
00:06:58,084 --> 00:06:59,619
This is delicious.

120
00:07:05,225 --> 00:07:07,127
-Oh!
-Oh, my goodness.

121
00:07:07,193 --> 00:07:10,297
Min-gi, what on earth happened to you?

122
00:07:10,363 --> 00:07:12,132
Were you okay at the station?

123
00:07:12,198 --> 00:07:15,235
Yes. I apologize for making you worry.

124
00:07:21,174 --> 00:07:23,843
-Oh, Yu-na.
-Can we talk?

125
00:07:42,896 --> 00:07:45,732
I'm sorry. I got angry despite myself…

126
00:07:45,799 --> 00:07:47,067
Min-gi.

127
00:07:47,767 --> 00:07:49,402
Let's go to Seoul.

128
00:07:49,469 --> 00:07:53,106
Huh? What do you mean all of a sudden?

129
00:07:53,173 --> 00:07:57,243
That whole thing has died down,
and I'm feeling suffocated here now.

130
00:07:57,310 --> 00:07:59,779
You don't need to stay here anymore.

131
00:07:59,846 --> 00:08:01,614
The cabbage farming's all over.

132
00:08:01,681 --> 00:08:03,216
What do you mean, over?

133
00:08:04,884 --> 00:08:06,219
It's not over yet.

134
00:08:08,188 --> 00:08:13,293
I'll release that album at all costs.

135
00:08:14,160 --> 00:08:16,229
I'm never giving up.

136
00:08:16,296 --> 00:08:20,066
If I give up now, I'll have nothing.

137
00:08:21,468 --> 00:08:24,637
Just like everyone else,
with no dreams and no hope,

138
00:08:24,704 --> 00:08:26,806
I'd probably just drift through life.

139
00:08:27,574 --> 00:08:31,378
But I'd rather die than do that.

140
00:08:31,444 --> 00:08:32,746
I won't live like that.

141
00:08:33,413 --> 00:08:35,148
If you want to go, go alone.

142
00:08:35,215 --> 00:08:36,983
I definitely can't go.

143
00:08:37,617 --> 00:08:39,285
No…

144
00:08:40,120 --> 00:08:41,755
I won't go.

145
00:08:51,464 --> 00:08:53,133
Gosh…

146
00:09:06,913 --> 00:09:08,181
It's not like that.

147
00:09:08,815 --> 00:09:12,152
It's not pity, and it's not sympathy.

148
00:09:12,819 --> 00:09:14,120
Then what is it?

149
00:09:14,187 --> 00:09:17,323
I don't know… what this feeling is.

150
00:09:18,024 --> 00:09:19,993
But it's not like that.

151
00:09:20,060 --> 00:09:21,428
I said it's not like that.

152
00:09:23,196 --> 00:09:24,330
Gosh.

153
00:09:30,970 --> 00:09:33,673
Min-gi, are you asleep?

154
00:09:34,607 --> 00:09:35,708
No, why?

155
00:09:41,047 --> 00:09:42,248
You know what…

156
00:09:45,251 --> 00:09:46,653
Actually, never mind.

157
00:09:47,253 --> 00:09:49,756
What? Why stop mid-sentence?

158
00:09:50,757 --> 00:09:52,258
What is it? Tell me.

159
00:09:53,693 --> 00:09:55,295
-I mean…
-Hey!

160
00:09:55,361 --> 00:09:57,797
Let's get some sleep! Just sleep!

161
00:09:57,864 --> 00:10:01,568
Don't we have to go to Seoul
at dawn to sell cabbages again?

162
00:10:04,604 --> 00:10:06,473
Okay, I get it.

163
00:10:08,308 --> 00:10:10,176
Let's just go to sleep.

164
00:10:21,921 --> 00:10:25,625
You scared me! You could've knocked.

165
00:10:25,692 --> 00:10:28,595
Knock? Since when have we done that?

166
00:10:29,362 --> 00:10:32,499
Why are you putting on a disguise
all of a sudden?

167
00:10:32,565 --> 00:10:35,502
-Are you going somewhere?
-No, just because.

168
00:10:36,436 --> 00:10:39,706
Why? Did you need something?

169
00:10:39,772 --> 00:10:42,542
Oh, I didn't need anything!

170
00:10:42,609 --> 00:10:44,244
Gosh…

171
00:10:46,446 --> 00:10:49,516
Um, hasn't I-ji contacted you either?

172
00:10:49,582 --> 00:10:51,885
No, she hasn't.

173
00:10:51,951 --> 00:10:54,521
Why? Are you worried about her?

174
00:10:54,587 --> 00:10:56,055
Worried, my foot!

175
00:10:56,122 --> 00:10:59,959
I don't even care at all
how that girl lives, not me!

176
00:11:00,026 --> 00:11:02,428
Tell her to come home or not,
as she likes!

177
00:11:02,495 --> 00:11:04,364
Good grief.

178
00:11:04,430 --> 00:11:06,666
He's clearly worried about her.

179
00:11:07,867 --> 00:11:10,770
Tomorrow's my first date with Mr. Han.

180
00:11:10,837 --> 00:11:12,705
My heart is fluttering.

181
00:11:13,773 --> 00:11:15,408
I need to look pretty.

182
00:11:15,475 --> 00:11:18,077
Should I have gotten more Botox?

183
00:11:33,860 --> 00:11:35,695
Mi-yeong!

184
00:11:35,762 --> 00:11:38,765
What's with how you look?
You're not even homeless.

185
00:11:39,265 --> 00:11:41,034
Stop this and just go home, babe.

186
00:11:41,100 --> 00:11:42,135
I can't.

187
00:11:42,202 --> 00:11:44,671
If I go home, my mom will kill me.

188
00:11:46,773 --> 00:11:50,143
Here, I bought you
a change of clothes and some socks.

189
00:11:51,444 --> 00:11:53,379
-Thanks, Mi-yeong.
-Whatever.

190
00:11:53,446 --> 00:11:55,682
Are you out of energy already?

191
00:11:55,748 --> 00:11:58,518
I'm just bursting with energy!

192
00:11:59,118 --> 00:12:03,289
Come here.
I'll give you a rib-crushing hug.

193
00:12:03,356 --> 00:12:04,490
No, thanks.

194
00:12:04,557 --> 00:12:06,826
What do you mean, no thanks?

195
00:12:06,893 --> 00:12:08,661
Get over here!

196
00:12:12,265 --> 00:12:15,702
Mi-yeong, even if it's hard now,
let's hang in there together.

197
00:12:16,369 --> 00:12:18,538
I promise I'll make you happy.

198
00:12:19,205 --> 00:12:21,674
I just have to convince Mom, just Mom.

199
00:12:21,741 --> 00:12:23,810
So just hang in there a bit…

200
00:12:25,345 --> 00:12:27,046
What's wrong?

201
00:12:30,083 --> 00:12:31,884
Eun-u!

202
00:12:32,552 --> 00:12:35,188
Eun-u! Eun-u!

203
00:12:35,255 --> 00:12:37,156
-Eun-u!

204
00:12:40,793 --> 00:12:42,262
Um, Eun-u.

205
00:12:42,328 --> 00:12:45,231
Forget it, stop.
I don't want to hear anything.

206
00:12:45,298 --> 00:12:47,767
I told you, I hate that man!

207
00:12:47,834 --> 00:12:49,135
Is it because of Dad?

208
00:12:49,202 --> 00:12:52,305
No, Dad married someone else too.

209
00:12:52,372 --> 00:12:55,608
I hope you meet someone nice
and get married too.

210
00:12:55,675 --> 00:12:57,043
But I hate that man.

211
00:12:57,110 --> 00:12:58,177
Why?

212
00:12:58,244 --> 00:13:00,213
I hate how he just drinks every day.

213
00:13:00,280 --> 00:13:03,616
I hate how he looks,
and I hate all his facial hair.

214
00:13:03,683 --> 00:13:05,918
And I hate how he talks. I hate it all.

215
00:13:05,985 --> 00:13:07,787
Even though I like him?

216
00:13:07,854 --> 00:13:09,789
I said I hate him! I really do!

217
00:13:09,856 --> 00:13:13,092
Mom, get out!
I don't want to talk to you.

218
00:13:24,170 --> 00:13:25,672
Um, honey.

219
00:13:25,738 --> 00:13:27,874
Don't you worry. I'm not giving up.

220
00:13:28,675 --> 00:13:31,644
I'll win Eun-u over,
so don't worry and head to work.

221
00:13:31,711 --> 00:13:33,446
Okay.

222
00:13:40,820 --> 00:13:42,355
Eun-u.

223
00:13:44,357 --> 00:13:46,726
Sorry, sorry. I'll come back later.

224
00:13:49,462 --> 00:13:51,664
I think she needs time to calm down.

225
00:13:51,731 --> 00:13:54,033
But Eun-u should be a baseball player.

226
00:13:54,100 --> 00:13:56,803
She's got outstanding pitch control.

227
00:14:00,306 --> 00:14:01,441
Buy some cabbage!

228
00:14:01,507 --> 00:14:02,742
ONE CABBAGE: 700 WON

229
00:14:02,809 --> 00:14:05,211
Ma'am, buy some fresh winter cabbage.

230
00:14:05,278 --> 00:14:06,913
Buy some cabbage.

231
00:14:07,780 --> 00:14:09,482
Buy some cabbage!

232
00:14:09,549 --> 00:14:12,051
Why is business so slow?

233
00:14:12,585 --> 00:14:15,555
Right. Why did you do that yesterday?

234
00:14:16,322 --> 00:14:19,392
Why did you go all the way there
just to punch that guy?

235
00:14:19,459 --> 00:14:21,227
Because it upset me.

236
00:14:21,294 --> 00:14:23,429
Why does Yun-hui's business upset you?

237
00:14:23,496 --> 00:14:24,564
Huh?

238
00:14:25,398 --> 00:14:28,901
I mean, well, it's just…

239
00:14:29,502 --> 00:14:32,805
Wait, you don't like Yun-hui, do you?

240
00:14:44,817 --> 00:14:47,019
Why is it so awkward? It was a joke.

241
00:14:47,086 --> 00:14:48,855
Did my joke go too far? Sorry.

242
00:14:48,921 --> 00:14:51,190
Quit joking and get back to work, man.

243
00:14:51,257 --> 00:14:53,760
We need to sell
at least one more cabbage.

244
00:14:54,994 --> 00:14:56,429
Buy some cabbage!

245
00:14:56,496 --> 00:14:59,832
While we older guys work hard,
that punk Ki-jun's in his room,

246
00:14:59,899 --> 00:15:02,034
taking it easy, eating pork trotters.

247
00:15:02,101 --> 00:15:04,137
-Right?
-Let's sell cabbage.

248
00:15:16,516 --> 00:15:19,051
-Who is it?
-Pork trotters delivery.

249
00:15:21,554 --> 00:15:22,688
That's 30,000 won.

250
00:15:22,755 --> 00:15:25,725
Why are you so late?
I ordered this ages ago.

251
00:15:25,792 --> 00:15:27,960
I'm sorry, I… got a little lost.

252
00:15:28,027 --> 00:15:30,062
Forget it.

253
00:15:44,444 --> 00:15:48,214
Hey, you went out on a delivery.
Why are you back so late?

254
00:15:48,281 --> 00:15:50,016
You know how many calls I got?

255
00:15:50,082 --> 00:15:51,617
What can I do if I'm lost?

256
00:15:51,684 --> 00:15:54,987
If only you'd learned to work
at the pork trotter shop first.

257
00:15:55,054 --> 00:15:57,957
Cabbage farming, my foot!
Gosh, it drives me crazy!

258
00:15:58,024 --> 00:16:00,726
Why bring up cabbages again right now?

259
00:16:00,793 --> 00:16:04,764
Forget it. Starting tomorrow,
go back to civil service cram school.

260
00:16:05,998 --> 00:16:07,266
What?

261
00:16:09,402 --> 00:16:13,005
I don't want you living your life
smelling like pork trotters too.

262
00:16:13,072 --> 00:16:15,441
Stop coming to the shop tomorrow.

263
00:16:16,242 --> 00:16:18,110
You just study hard.

264
00:17:00,620 --> 00:17:02,388
Aw, thinking about your girl?

265
00:17:02,455 --> 00:17:06,092
Look how slick your face looks
after a little time in Seoul.

266
00:17:06,759 --> 00:17:09,228
Hey, feels good ditching us?

267
00:17:09,295 --> 00:17:10,730
Good? Good? Good? Like it?

268
00:17:10,796 --> 00:17:12,832
Stop it.

269
00:17:12,899 --> 00:17:15,668
-What brings you guys here?
-What do you think, man?

270
00:17:15,735 --> 00:17:18,037
We came to bring you cabbages, punk.

271
00:17:20,072 --> 00:17:22,441
-No, thanks.
-Hey, take it, man.

272
00:17:22,508 --> 00:17:24,243
We're giving you your share.

273
00:17:24,310 --> 00:17:26,412
Hey, and tell your mother

274
00:17:26,479 --> 00:17:28,981
never to worry about
this pork shop's cabbages.

275
00:17:31,350 --> 00:17:33,586
-Going well?
-Hardly. We're just

276
00:17:33,653 --> 00:17:36,389
struggling desperately to survive.

277
00:17:38,357 --> 00:17:39,325
I'm sorry.

278
00:17:39,392 --> 00:17:41,827
Forget it, man. I'm more sorry.

279
00:17:42,728 --> 00:17:45,298
Anyway, learn to run
the pork trotter shop well.

280
00:17:45,364 --> 00:17:47,099
-We're heading out.
-Okay.

281
00:17:47,166 --> 00:17:48,134
Hang in there.

282
00:17:48,200 --> 00:17:49,702
Let's go.

283
00:17:51,671 --> 00:17:54,273
See you.

284
00:17:54,340 --> 00:17:56,309
See you, man.

285
00:18:11,090 --> 00:18:13,993
Now, is this gal doing okay or what?

286
00:18:18,297 --> 00:18:19,932
Ow!

287
00:18:36,916 --> 00:18:39,185
We spent all day selling them,

288
00:18:39,251 --> 00:18:42,021
and we didn't even sell
a third, let alone half.

289
00:18:42,088 --> 00:18:45,224
Shouldn't we really give up now?

290
00:18:45,291 --> 00:18:46,959
What are you saying, man?

291
00:18:47,026 --> 00:18:49,762
Don't you know what Coach An said?

292
00:18:49,829 --> 00:18:51,197
Coach An?

293
00:18:53,466 --> 00:18:55,401
Oooooh!

294
00:18:55,468 --> 00:18:58,371
The moment you give up
is the moment the game ends.

295
00:18:58,437 --> 00:19:00,339
Oooooh!

296
00:19:01,140 --> 00:19:04,443
He left us with such a priceless quote.

297
00:19:04,510 --> 00:19:06,946
Coach An
of Shohoku High School basketball.

298
00:19:08,881 --> 00:19:10,182
Was that from a comic?

299
00:19:10,249 --> 00:19:13,619
But for us not to give up,

300
00:19:13,686 --> 00:19:16,355
our situation is way too bleak.

301
00:19:17,023 --> 00:19:21,661
I worked myself half to death
thinking only about the album.

302
00:19:22,161 --> 00:19:24,997
I never thought my life
would end so pathetically.

303
00:19:25,064 --> 00:19:27,900
Your life isn't ending so pathetically.

304
00:19:27,967 --> 00:19:30,202
You get a bit pessimistic sometimes.

305
00:19:33,072 --> 00:19:33,939
Guys!

306
00:19:34,006 --> 00:19:36,709
-You startled me.
-What brings you here again?

307
00:19:36,776 --> 00:19:39,145
Is it weird if a manager
visits her singers?

308
00:19:43,049 --> 00:19:45,751
Guys, it's not time to give up yet.

309
00:19:45,818 --> 00:19:47,086
We still have a chance.

310
00:19:47,153 --> 00:19:49,689
A chance? What chance?

311
00:19:49,755 --> 00:19:54,360
The Divorce Slap Video
passed seven million views today.

312
00:19:54,427 --> 00:19:57,296
Demand for a follow-up is still huge.

313
00:19:57,363 --> 00:19:58,431
That again?

314
00:19:59,565 --> 00:20:01,701
Anyway, people are so weird.

315
00:20:01,767 --> 00:20:04,870
What's so great about it
that people keep watching it?

316
00:20:04,937 --> 00:20:07,973
Whoa, don't underestimate the internet.

317
00:20:08,040 --> 00:20:11,077
Use it right, and anything can happen.

318
00:20:11,143 --> 00:20:14,180
Who knows?
You might even get to release an album.

319
00:20:14,246 --> 00:20:17,717
Ha, an album? How?

320
00:20:17,783 --> 00:20:22,188
Guys, don't you know
how many people became internet stars?

321
00:20:22,254 --> 00:20:25,524
Trust me, this is totally possible.

322
00:20:28,294 --> 00:20:30,863
That's just their story.

323
00:20:30,930 --> 00:20:34,867
So you're just going to give up
and live like useless bums again?

324
00:20:35,468 --> 00:20:39,205
Miracles never come
to those who just sit still.

325
00:20:39,271 --> 00:20:40,806
Don't you know that saying?

326
00:20:41,741 --> 00:20:43,476
We have to try something.

327
00:20:43,542 --> 00:20:46,946
Does sitting around sighing
put food on the table? Right?

328
00:20:47,012 --> 00:20:49,348
Huh? Uh…

329
00:20:50,850 --> 00:20:53,185
Well, the thing is…

330
00:20:58,190 --> 00:21:00,493
Can we really film
looking this ridiculous?

331
00:21:00,559 --> 00:21:04,997
Yes! It's fresh, natural, and charming.

332
00:21:05,064 --> 00:21:07,566
And what people want from you guys

333
00:21:07,633 --> 00:21:10,069
isn't anything normal.

334
00:21:12,004 --> 00:21:14,940
Fine, my image is ruined,
so do whatever you want.

335
00:21:15,007 --> 00:21:19,245
Okay, recording starts now.

336
00:21:19,845 --> 00:21:22,281
One, two, three.

337
00:21:45,404 --> 00:21:49,074
When love comes without me knowing

338
00:21:49,141 --> 00:21:52,545
When love comes like a dream

339
00:21:52,611 --> 00:21:57,249
Holding me close every time I see you

340
00:21:57,850 --> 00:22:01,720
I just smile in pure happiness

341
00:22:02,721 --> 00:22:05,591
Can you hear my heart?

342
00:22:05,658 --> 00:22:09,595
Shall I send it on the wind?

343
00:22:11,730 --> 00:22:16,302
With the word love filling the world

344
00:22:16,368 --> 00:22:18,237
As it colors everything

345
00:22:19,505 --> 00:22:22,241
I'll wait for you, I love you

346
00:22:22,308 --> 00:22:26,478
It will carry my words to you

347
00:22:31,951 --> 00:22:34,153
Cut! Okay!

348
00:22:34,220 --> 00:22:36,555
This is so embarrassing. What is this?

349
00:22:36,622 --> 00:22:38,824
It's okay, it's okay.

350
00:22:38,891 --> 00:22:42,895
The moment this drops,
what are you? Universal Superstars!

351
00:22:42,962 --> 00:22:44,830
Universal Superstars?

352
00:22:45,464 --> 00:22:46,999
I don't buy it.

353
00:22:47,066 --> 00:22:49,602
But guys, your music video concept

354
00:22:49,668 --> 00:22:52,037
doesn't match your band name at all.

355
00:22:52,104 --> 00:22:54,773
While you're at it,
why not change your band name?

356
00:22:54,840 --> 00:22:56,842
Do whatever you want, Manager.

357
00:22:58,244 --> 00:22:59,912
What would be good?

358
00:23:07,253 --> 00:23:09,622
The Farmers! How about The Farmers?

359
00:23:09,688 --> 00:23:13,192
What is this, the '80s?
We're not Kang Byung-chul and Samtaegi.

360
00:23:13,259 --> 00:23:14,894
The Farmers? Seriously?

361
00:23:14,960 --> 00:23:16,161
You think so?

362
00:23:16,228 --> 00:23:18,097
Well, then…

363
00:23:18,163 --> 00:23:22,001
Farmers? Or just Farmer?

364
00:23:22,067 --> 00:23:24,870
The Farmers, Farmer, Farmers…
It's all the same.

365
00:23:24,937 --> 00:23:26,939
These names all sound too outdated.

366
00:23:27,006 --> 00:23:29,642
Isn't there anything more modern?

367
00:23:30,142 --> 00:23:31,877
Something modern…

368
00:23:33,045 --> 00:23:35,581
Modern Farmer, Modern Farmer!

369
00:23:35,648 --> 00:23:38,851
How about Modern Farmer?
Farmers who play modern rock.

370
00:23:38,918 --> 00:23:41,587
What did you say? Modern Farmer?

371
00:23:41,654 --> 00:23:43,756
Oh!

372
00:23:43,822 --> 00:23:45,324
Sounds stylish, doesn't it?

373
00:23:45,391 --> 00:23:46,825
That's good. I like it.

374
00:23:46,892 --> 00:23:49,261
Rolls right off the tongue.
Modern Farmer.

375
00:23:49,328 --> 00:23:50,529
Okay!

376
00:23:50,596 --> 00:23:54,700
Now, Modern Farmer's first music video

377
00:23:54,767 --> 00:23:56,869
is being uploaded right now!

378
00:24:02,441 --> 00:24:03,809
DAD: AREN'T YOU COMING?

379
00:24:04,910 --> 00:24:06,278
It's my dad.

380
00:24:06,345 --> 00:24:09,515
Guys, I'm running late. I should go.

381
00:24:11,951 --> 00:24:16,255
I'll upload it tonight,
so expect an explosive reaction!

382
00:24:18,357 --> 00:24:20,225
See you.

383
00:24:21,727 --> 00:24:22,828
Will this work?

384
00:24:22,895 --> 00:24:24,863
Don't get your hopes up.

385
00:24:26,532 --> 00:24:28,534
Then what if we're really done for?

386
00:24:28,600 --> 00:24:33,772
I really wish a chunk of gold
would just fall right out of the sky.

387
00:24:55,995 --> 00:24:59,331
What is this? Who did this?

388
00:25:05,971 --> 00:25:08,340
Which damned bastard pulled this?

389
00:25:17,249 --> 00:25:21,653
Even if we haul the cabbages up,
we clearly won't even cover gas.

390
00:25:21,720 --> 00:25:24,023
This is seriously driving me crazy.

391
00:25:24,089 --> 00:25:25,591
Jeez…

392
00:25:26,392 --> 00:25:27,426
What's that?

393
00:25:28,060 --> 00:25:29,595
Did something happen there?

394
00:25:31,430 --> 00:25:33,132
So, how did you discover it?

395
00:25:33,198 --> 00:25:35,701
When I came out this morning,

396
00:25:35,768 --> 00:25:39,071
a huge hole was blown right
through the greenhouse roof.

397
00:25:39,138 --> 00:25:41,874
This rock had fallen
in the middle of the field.

398
00:25:42,541 --> 00:25:46,879
At first, I thought
some damned bastard did this and left.

399
00:25:46,945 --> 00:25:47,813
But…

400
00:25:50,249 --> 00:25:52,918
who could've known it was a meteorite?

401
00:25:54,153 --> 00:25:55,020
What is that?

402
00:25:55,087 --> 00:25:56,889
Doctor, what do you think?

403
00:25:56,955 --> 00:26:00,659
We'll need to examine it closely
to know the exact details, but

404
00:26:00,726 --> 00:26:02,861
visually, it's definitely a meteorite.

405
00:26:02,928 --> 00:26:05,564
Then how much is this meteorite worth?

406
00:26:05,631 --> 00:26:08,267
Again, we'd need to test it
to know for sure,

407
00:26:08,333 --> 00:26:12,137
but the price of this meteorite
varies widely depending on its type.

408
00:26:12,204 --> 00:26:15,641
For example, that rare meteorite
that fell in Russia

409
00:26:15,707 --> 00:26:18,677
is known to be worth
over tens of billions of won.

410
00:26:18,744 --> 00:26:20,446
This meteorite's worth at least

411
00:26:20,512 --> 00:26:23,148
several hundred million won, I believe.

412
00:26:24,316 --> 00:26:27,219
Experts predict that more
meteorite fragments

413
00:26:27,286 --> 00:26:30,055
are likely to be found nearby.

414
00:26:30,122 --> 00:26:32,558
Already in Hadurong-ri,
meteorite hunters

415
00:26:32,624 --> 00:26:35,294
have been gathering here one by one
since morning.

416
00:26:35,360 --> 00:26:36,662
From Hadurong-ri…

417
00:26:36,728 --> 00:26:38,363
So that one chunk of rock

418
00:26:38,430 --> 00:26:41,066
is worth more than
100,000 heads of cabbage?

419
00:26:45,671 --> 00:26:46,638
Right.

420
00:26:50,442 --> 00:26:51,310
Ma'am!

421
00:26:51,376 --> 00:26:53,545
Don't, don't, don't!

422
00:26:53,612 --> 00:26:56,181
Min-gi, didn't you guys go
to sell cabbages?

423
00:26:56,248 --> 00:26:57,649
Yu-na, a meteorite fell here!

424
00:26:57,716 --> 00:26:58,584
A meteorite!

425
00:26:58,650 --> 00:27:00,452
A meteorite?

426
00:27:00,519 --> 00:27:02,254
Yes! If we find that meteorite,

427
00:27:02,321 --> 00:27:03,722
we can release our album!

428
00:27:03,789 --> 00:27:06,191
Wait, wait! Where are the work gloves?

429
00:27:06,258 --> 00:27:07,826
Work gloves for what now?

430
00:27:07,893 --> 00:27:09,528
If we have to shovel all day,

431
00:27:09,595 --> 00:27:11,497
shouldn't we be fully prepared?

432
00:27:11,563 --> 00:27:12,431
Ma'am, where?

433
00:27:12,498 --> 00:27:15,033
They're in the first drawer there.

434
00:27:15,100 --> 00:27:15,968
I found them!

435
00:27:16,034 --> 00:27:17,503
Thank you!

436
00:27:18,770 --> 00:27:22,407
Gosh, how hectic.
A meteorite all of a sudden?

437
00:27:22,474 --> 00:27:25,511
I know. That's another strange thing.

438
00:27:25,577 --> 00:27:28,714
By the way, Yun-hui,
what have you been doing?

439
00:27:28,780 --> 00:27:30,215
Me?

440
00:27:30,282 --> 00:27:31,216
www.6차산업.com

441
00:27:31,283 --> 00:27:32,718
On a sixth industry site,

442
00:27:32,784 --> 00:27:35,921
I'm looking up what we can do
with Min-gi's cabbages.

443
00:27:35,988 --> 00:27:39,324
Cabbage prices have crashed.
Could there be any way?

444
00:27:39,391 --> 00:27:41,426
Come on, even if cabbage prices fell,

445
00:27:41,493 --> 00:27:42,961
we can sell salted cabbage,

446
00:27:43,028 --> 00:27:45,097
make winter kimchi to sell,

447
00:27:45,164 --> 00:27:47,599
or run a kimchi
Rural Experience Village.

448
00:27:47,666 --> 00:27:50,402
They help people pursuing
the sixth industry

449
00:27:50,469 --> 00:27:51,737
with low-interest loans

450
00:27:51,803 --> 00:27:53,839
and provide consulting too.

451
00:27:53,906 --> 00:27:55,541
You seem worried too, Yun-hui.

452
00:27:56,441 --> 00:27:58,076
Yes, I am.

453
00:27:58,143 --> 00:28:01,113
They're struggling so hard
just to release one album.

454
00:28:01,180 --> 00:28:04,183
We should help in any way we can.

455
00:28:31,210 --> 00:28:33,579
-It's me.
-Why are you calling?

456
00:28:33,645 --> 00:28:35,280
You acted like we were done.

457
00:28:35,347 --> 00:28:36,982
I'll come back.

458
00:28:37,049 --> 00:28:39,017
Really? Smart choice.

459
00:28:39,084 --> 00:28:42,955
But I have one condition.

460
00:28:51,230 --> 00:28:54,166
Hey, what on earth
are all those people doing?

461
00:28:54,233 --> 00:28:58,237
I know.
What are they digging for like that?

462
00:28:58,303 --> 00:28:59,871
I'm late!

463
00:29:00,973 --> 00:29:03,675
-You're doing great!
-Hi, Su-yeon!

464
00:29:03,742 --> 00:29:04,743
-Han-cheol
-Su-yeon.

465
00:29:04,810 --> 00:29:06,044
Where are you rushing?

466
00:29:06,111 --> 00:29:08,380
They say a meteorite hit our village!

467
00:29:08,447 --> 00:29:09,381
A meteorite?

468
00:29:09,448 --> 00:29:11,316
Yes, I'm on my way to find it now.

469
00:29:11,383 --> 00:29:13,852
They say each one's worth
hundreds of millions!

470
00:29:13,919 --> 00:29:17,456
If I find it, I'll definitely
open a clothing shop for you.

471
00:29:18,190 --> 00:29:19,891
Bye! I'm off!

472
00:29:20,559 --> 00:29:22,027
A meteorite out of nowhere?

473
00:29:22,928 --> 00:29:24,863
Forget it. Never mind.

474
00:29:24,930 --> 00:29:27,199
Since when has he ever been normal?

475
00:29:27,266 --> 00:29:28,834
Let's just go paint.

476
00:29:28,900 --> 00:29:30,402
Wait a second!

477
00:29:30,469 --> 00:29:33,405
What if they keep digging
and find the five billion?

478
00:29:35,073 --> 00:29:37,709
-You're right.
-We can't let that happen.

479
00:29:37,776 --> 00:29:39,211
What do we do?

480
00:29:39,278 --> 00:29:42,080
What else can we do?
We have no choice now.

481
00:29:42,147 --> 00:29:43,782
Screw the wall or who sees us!

482
00:29:43,849 --> 00:29:45,484
We must find the money fast.

483
00:29:45,550 --> 00:29:46,985
What are you doing? Hurry!

484
00:29:47,052 --> 00:29:48,687
Okay, okay.

485
00:29:51,089 --> 00:29:53,492
ALWAYS FAST NEWS HD TV

486
00:30:03,201 --> 00:30:05,871
Meteorite, where are you?

487
00:30:05,937 --> 00:30:07,773
Meteorite…

488
00:30:09,341 --> 00:30:10,776
Huh?

489
00:30:10,842 --> 00:30:12,010
Sir!

490
00:30:12,077 --> 00:30:13,178
Hello!

491
00:30:13,245 --> 00:30:14,880
Hello, sir.

492
00:30:15,781 --> 00:30:17,182
Here for a meteorite too?

493
00:30:17,249 --> 00:30:19,551
Yes, why? Can't I look for one?

494
00:30:19,618 --> 00:30:21,053
That's not what I meant.

495
00:30:21,119 --> 00:30:23,689
You're surprisingly greedy
for money too, sir.

496
00:30:23,755 --> 00:30:25,824
What'll you do with money at your age?

497
00:30:25,891 --> 00:30:26,958
Me?

498
00:30:27,025 --> 00:30:28,827
To buy this chocolate bar.

499
00:30:28,894 --> 00:30:30,128
What?

500
00:30:30,195 --> 00:30:32,397
Hunting meteorites
to buy a chocolate bar?

501
00:30:32,464 --> 00:30:33,332
Yes.

502
00:30:33,398 --> 00:30:36,335
I'll give you all the almonds later.

503
00:30:36,401 --> 00:30:37,769
No, thanks! Forget it!

504
00:30:37,836 --> 00:30:40,906
Why are those people doing this to me?

505
00:30:42,240 --> 00:30:44,042
Oh? Su-yeon!

506
00:30:45,077 --> 00:30:46,478
Let's find the meteorite.

507
00:30:46,545 --> 00:30:48,113
Su-yeon!

508
00:30:48,180 --> 00:30:50,816
Su-yeon, you're digging here again.

509
00:30:51,416 --> 00:30:53,151
You came for the meteorite too?

510
00:30:53,218 --> 00:30:55,220
Um, yes, I guess.

511
00:30:55,287 --> 00:30:56,488
Oh, honestly.

512
00:30:56,555 --> 00:30:58,890
I promised you a clothing shop
if I find it.

513
00:30:58,957 --> 00:31:00,592
You should just wait a bit.

514
00:31:01,393 --> 00:31:04,396
Anyway, this thing called human greed

515
00:31:04,463 --> 00:31:06,431
really has no end, no end at all.

516
00:31:07,866 --> 00:31:09,701
I suppose that's true.

517
00:31:09,768 --> 00:31:12,437
Yu-na, let's go that way. That way.

518
00:31:12,504 --> 00:31:14,039
Let's go that way, then.

519
00:31:14,106 --> 00:31:16,341
Han-cheol, please handle this spot.

520
00:31:16,408 --> 00:31:18,777
Yes, go right ahead, then!

521
00:31:22,647 --> 00:31:25,517
It's crazy, just crazy.
This spot looks good, right?

522
00:31:25,584 --> 00:31:27,219
Where should we go?

523
00:31:32,023 --> 00:31:33,892
Hadurong-ri, the meteorite site,

524
00:31:33,959 --> 00:31:37,396
is still bustling with citizens
hoping to find a meteorite.

525
00:31:38,897 --> 00:31:41,767
I'll do your homework for life.

526
00:31:41,833 --> 00:31:44,369
Korean, English, math,
even art, all of it.

527
00:31:45,003 --> 00:31:48,740
Plus, I'll make your favorite
sausage dish every day.

528
00:31:48,807 --> 00:31:50,242
And my face…

529
00:31:52,444 --> 00:31:55,080
Fine, what the heck, I'll get surgery.

530
00:31:55,147 --> 00:31:57,649
Who do you like? Hyun Bin? Won Bin?

531
00:31:59,217 --> 00:32:02,154
This deal is practically like
trading away my own life.

532
00:32:02,220 --> 00:32:05,123
Listen closely.
Eun-u, if you just accept me,

533
00:32:05,190 --> 00:32:06,958
starting today…

534
00:32:10,529 --> 00:32:12,197
I'll even quit drinking.

535
00:32:12,764 --> 00:32:15,100
You really have to give me credit.

536
00:32:15,167 --> 00:32:16,868
I've drunk since grade school,

537
00:32:16,935 --> 00:32:19,337
so breaking up with it is not easy.

538
00:32:20,338 --> 00:32:22,808
This is driving me crazy, really.

539
00:32:22,874 --> 00:32:25,277
Then what am I supposed to do?

540
00:32:25,343 --> 00:32:26,445
Eun-u.

541
00:32:26,511 --> 00:32:30,782
I really love your mom.

542
00:32:30,849 --> 00:32:34,586
I mean it. I'll make your mom and you

543
00:32:34,653 --> 00:32:36,354
happy for the rest of my life.

544
00:32:36,421 --> 00:32:38,056
Okay?

545
00:32:40,325 --> 00:32:42,327
Come on, don't be like that.

546
00:32:50,569 --> 00:32:52,237
Um, Eun-u.

547
00:32:53,472 --> 00:32:56,475
I'm leaving. I was about to leave.

548
00:32:58,009 --> 00:32:59,744
Do you maybe like baseball?

549
00:33:02,347 --> 00:33:03,582
All right.

550
00:33:03,648 --> 00:33:05,317
Get plenty of rest.

551
00:33:08,920 --> 00:33:10,222
Welcome…

552
00:33:13,692 --> 00:33:15,927
What are you doing here?

553
00:33:15,994 --> 00:33:18,396
Why? Am I not allowed to come here?

554
00:33:18,463 --> 00:33:21,967
How long will you live like this?
Aren't you coming home?

555
00:33:22,033 --> 00:33:25,704
I told you I'd never go home
until I save up to open a coffee shop.

556
00:33:25,770 --> 00:33:28,874
How will you ever open a cafe
working part-time, you brat!

557
00:33:28,940 --> 00:33:31,276
I'll handle it, so you butt out.

558
00:33:31,343 --> 00:33:34,312
Fine, I wish I could butt out. Gosh.

559
00:33:40,952 --> 00:33:41,987
Here.

560
00:33:42,053 --> 00:33:43,688
What is this?

561
00:33:45,090 --> 00:33:47,125
Wait, did you really disown me?

562
00:33:47,192 --> 00:33:50,161
Open it and you'll see. Just open it.

563
00:33:56,835 --> 00:34:00,639
E COFFEE FRANCHISE AGREEMENT

564
00:34:00,705 --> 00:34:04,209
This… is this for real?

565
00:34:04,276 --> 00:34:07,946
It's not free.
Pay a little each month with interest.

566
00:34:08,013 --> 00:34:10,348
Fall behind once
and I close the shop that day.

567
00:34:10,415 --> 00:34:11,283
Got it?

568
00:34:12,050 --> 00:34:15,253
Really?
Are you really opening a cafe for me?

569
00:34:15,320 --> 00:34:18,890
I leased the very best spot in Seoul.

570
00:34:18,957 --> 00:34:21,259
-Do a good job.
-Oh, Man-gu.

571
00:34:21,326 --> 00:34:24,696
If you're doing this,
do it right in Seoul. Do it right.

572
00:34:24,763 --> 00:34:27,599
Thank you, I love you!

573
00:34:27,666 --> 00:34:29,801
Gross, why are you being like this?

574
00:34:30,635 --> 00:34:32,170
Pack up so we can go home.

575
00:34:32,237 --> 00:34:34,039
Okay!

576
00:34:36,575 --> 00:34:37,876
Is she that happy?

577
00:34:37,943 --> 00:34:40,178
She's jumping for joy, jumping for joy.

578
00:34:41,246 --> 00:34:42,314
As I always feel,

579
00:34:42,380 --> 00:34:45,317
coming to a temple calms my mind.

580
00:34:46,217 --> 00:34:48,420
But today, my heart won't calm down.

581
00:34:48,486 --> 00:34:49,788
Why is that?

582
00:34:51,990 --> 00:34:53,558
Because of you, Ms. Kim.

583
00:34:53,625 --> 00:34:57,028
Oh my, oh my. Aren't you a funny man?

584
00:35:00,732 --> 00:35:01,900
I'm only joking.

585
00:35:01,967 --> 00:35:04,402
Oh, I don't know anymore.

586
00:35:06,004 --> 00:35:08,807
Let's bow while we're here, Ms. Kim.

587
00:35:08,873 --> 00:35:11,009
Yes.

588
00:35:30,362 --> 00:35:32,130
Oh, did he hear it?

589
00:35:34,366 --> 00:35:37,068
Maybe he didn't hear it.
Gosh, how embarrassing.

590
00:35:37,135 --> 00:35:40,438
Why have I been so gassy all morning?

591
00:35:56,187 --> 00:35:57,922
He definitely heard it.

592
00:37:00,418 --> 00:37:02,253
I heard they're dense and heavy.

593
00:37:02,320 --> 00:37:04,789
And they say most are dark red.

594
00:37:04,856 --> 00:37:06,558
I looked it all up, of course.

595
00:37:06,624 --> 00:37:08,560
Aren't you something.

596
00:37:08,626 --> 00:37:11,096
But is there even a meteorite here?

597
00:37:14,499 --> 00:37:16,534
Guys, come over here!

598
00:37:16,601 --> 00:37:18,336
You come over here.

599
00:37:18,403 --> 00:37:20,138
Seriously, give me a break.

600
00:37:21,639 --> 00:37:23,174
It's not sticking.

601
00:37:23,241 --> 00:37:24,509
How'd you get a magnet?

602
00:37:24,576 --> 00:37:27,212
I can find anything.
This town has everything.

603
00:37:28,680 --> 00:37:29,714
Jeez, seriously.

604
00:37:29,781 --> 00:37:32,617
Look at this.
Isn't it different from other rocks?

605
00:37:32,684 --> 00:37:35,887
Right, to call it just a rock,
it does look pretty unusual…

606
00:37:38,656 --> 00:37:40,325
No way.

607
00:37:41,126 --> 00:37:42,460
A meteorite?

608
00:37:42,527 --> 00:37:45,029
I heard meteorites are dense and heavy.

609
00:37:45,096 --> 00:37:46,498
Was that heavy?

610
00:37:47,132 --> 00:37:49,134
-It's heavy! So heavy!
-Really?

611
00:37:49,200 --> 00:37:51,369
They say meteorites are dark red.

612
00:37:51,436 --> 00:37:52,437
Is this dark red?

613
00:37:52,504 --> 00:37:54,672
Look at this. It's dark red! Dark red!

614
00:37:55,673 --> 00:37:57,142
It's dark red. Hey, wait.

615
00:37:58,309 --> 00:38:00,779
They say it's full of iron,
so magnets stick.

616
00:38:00,845 --> 00:38:02,781
Hey, put the magnet on it.

617
00:38:02,847 --> 00:38:04,849
The magnet.

618
00:38:07,519 --> 00:38:10,889
I'm too nervous to do it.
You do it, Gorilla.

619
00:38:13,158 --> 00:38:15,527
Wait, let's say a prayer first.

620
00:38:26,704 --> 00:38:28,373
It stuck!

621
00:38:28,439 --> 00:38:30,275
It stuck! It really stuck!

622
00:38:30,341 --> 00:38:32,076
Hey, we found it!

623
00:38:36,915 --> 00:38:39,217
Hey, wait. Is this really a meteorite?

624
00:38:39,284 --> 00:38:40,552
It is, right?

625
00:38:40,618 --> 00:38:42,954
Come on, man. When I sent a photo,

626
00:38:43,021 --> 00:38:45,957
the expert said it's over 90% certain.

627
00:38:46,024 --> 00:38:47,859
-Hey!
-It's 100% for sure!

628
00:38:47,926 --> 00:38:49,794
Hey, if it weren't, that expert

629
00:38:49,861 --> 00:38:52,096
wouldn't be dying to buy it in person.

630
00:38:53,164 --> 00:38:54,532
Our struggles are over.

631
00:38:54,599 --> 00:38:55,600
No more struggles.

632
00:38:55,667 --> 00:38:58,536
Our struggles are finally over!

633
00:38:59,270 --> 00:39:02,073
Let's hurry up, sell this,
and work on our album.

634
00:39:02,140 --> 00:39:05,643
Aw, so pretty, our little lucky charm.

635
00:39:05,710 --> 00:39:08,079
At times like this,
we have to be careful.

636
00:39:08,146 --> 00:39:10,315
That's when bad luck always strikes.

637
00:39:10,381 --> 00:39:13,818
The roads are icy today,
so drive carefully, man.

638
00:39:13,885 --> 00:39:15,920
What? We have to go sell it fast.

639
00:39:15,987 --> 00:39:17,689
Hold on tight, I'm flooring it!

640
00:39:17,755 --> 00:39:19,390
Hey!

641
00:39:21,659 --> 00:39:22,794
Why's it doing this?

642
00:39:22,861 --> 00:39:24,929
-Hey, what's wrong?
-What's happening?

643
00:39:38,309 --> 00:39:40,478
Wait… Uh, right now,

644
00:39:40,545 --> 00:39:43,815
uh, if we move forward even a little,

645
00:39:43,882 --> 00:39:46,384
it might fall right into the water.

646
00:39:46,451 --> 00:39:48,920
See, I told you to drive carefully!

647
00:39:48,987 --> 00:39:51,489
Hey, wait. Right now, luckily,

648
00:39:51,556 --> 00:39:53,124
with the cabbages in back,

649
00:39:53,191 --> 00:39:55,627
the weight makes the back heavier,

650
00:39:55,693 --> 00:39:57,495
so we're barely holding on.

651
00:39:57,562 --> 00:40:00,632
Let's slowly shift our weight back.

652
00:40:00,698 --> 00:40:03,301
-Back?
-Back, slowly back.

653
00:40:06,337 --> 00:40:10,508
Back, back, slowly.
It's okay, it's okay, it's okay.

654
00:40:13,945 --> 00:40:16,281
Hey, now's when we have to stay calm!

655
00:40:16,347 --> 00:40:19,951
I'll call 119 right now, so hold on.

656
00:40:20,018 --> 00:40:22,053
Where is it? My cell phone?

657
00:40:24,722 --> 00:40:28,760
Hello? Yes, yes, sir! Is this 119?

658
00:40:28,826 --> 00:40:32,830
Yes, we just went off some cliff.

659
00:40:32,897 --> 00:40:35,333
We're dangling precariously right now.

660
00:40:38,202 --> 00:40:39,938
Please save us! Please save us!

661
00:40:40,004 --> 00:40:42,273
Save us! There's water right below us.

662
00:40:42,340 --> 00:40:43,942
I'll just leave my phone on.

663
00:40:44,008 --> 00:40:45,009
Trace our location!

664
00:40:45,076 --> 00:40:47,712
Trace us! We don't know where we are.

665
00:40:47,779 --> 00:40:50,114
Please save us! Please save us!

666
00:40:55,987 --> 00:40:58,589
Hey, isn't it tilting more than before?

667
00:40:58,656 --> 00:40:59,524
It is tilting.

668
00:40:59,590 --> 00:41:01,225
Hey, it's tilting even more.

669
00:41:01,292 --> 00:41:02,460
What do we do?

670
00:41:02,527 --> 00:41:05,296
The front is heavier
than the cabbages in the back.

671
00:41:05,363 --> 00:41:07,398
I think that's why it's tilting more.

672
00:41:07,465 --> 00:41:09,734
We must lighten the front. The front!

673
00:41:09,801 --> 00:41:10,668
How?

674
00:41:10,735 --> 00:41:13,871
First, let's take off our clothes
and throw them out.

675
00:41:13,938 --> 00:41:16,341
We have to shed even a little weight.

676
00:41:19,243 --> 00:41:20,912
Hold on.

677
00:41:21,746 --> 00:41:23,881
Don't move! Don't move!

678
00:41:38,930 --> 00:41:40,198
Take off more, slowly.

679
00:41:40,264 --> 00:41:42,000
Take off even more?

680
00:41:42,066 --> 00:41:45,436
Hey, haven't we taken off enough now?

681
00:41:45,937 --> 00:41:48,373
-Take it off! Hurry!

682
00:41:48,439 --> 00:41:50,375
-Take it off! Fast!
-Will this work?

683
00:41:50,441 --> 00:41:52,710
Hurry! Hurry, hurry!

684
00:41:52,777 --> 00:41:54,512
Take it all off! Shoes too! Shoes!

685
00:41:55,313 --> 00:41:57,582
Take all of mine off too! All of it!

686
00:41:57,648 --> 00:42:00,018
Take off your shoes too! Shoes!

687
00:42:04,856 --> 00:42:07,258
Hey, your pants! Take your pants off!

688
00:42:07,325 --> 00:42:08,559
My pants? How can I?

689
00:42:08,626 --> 00:42:11,062
-Why do I have to strip?
-Take them off! Now!

690
00:42:12,630 --> 00:42:13,898
Do I strip first too?

691
00:42:13,965 --> 00:42:15,867
Take it all off properly!

692
00:42:15,933 --> 00:42:17,869
Wait a second.

693
00:42:27,245 --> 00:42:29,213
What are you doing right now?

694
00:42:29,280 --> 00:42:32,250
I'm spitting to lose some more weight.

695
00:42:32,316 --> 00:42:34,385
Ew, what's wrong with you?

696
00:42:40,658 --> 00:42:41,592
We tossed it all.

697
00:42:41,659 --> 00:42:42,927
Why's it doing this?

698
00:42:42,994 --> 00:42:44,295
Why's it still tilting?

699
00:42:44,362 --> 00:42:46,264
Hey, we have to shed more weight!

700
00:42:46,330 --> 00:42:48,666
We tossed it all! How do we shed more?

701
00:42:48,733 --> 00:42:50,668
There's nothing left to throw out.

702
00:42:51,169 --> 00:42:52,804
Nothing left to throw out?

703
00:42:55,540 --> 00:42:58,576
Hey, what are you staring at?

704
00:42:58,643 --> 00:43:00,278
Don't tell me you…

705
00:43:00,812 --> 00:43:04,315
That's a meteorite, you idiot!

706
00:43:04,382 --> 00:43:05,850
It's worth billions!

707
00:43:05,917 --> 00:43:09,320
And without this,
we can't release our album, man!

708
00:43:09,387 --> 00:43:11,355
Not this one. No way, never.

709
00:43:11,422 --> 00:43:13,424
Hey, you two, think straight.

710
00:43:13,491 --> 00:43:15,960
It beats releasing an album
in the afterlife.

711
00:43:16,027 --> 00:43:20,098
This little guy flew light-years
through space! Light-years!

712
00:43:20,164 --> 00:43:24,068
If we don't throw that out,
we'll die light-years early!

713
00:43:24,135 --> 00:43:25,803
Toss it, or it's the afterlife!

714
00:43:25,870 --> 00:43:28,072
Still, even with nothing left to toss,

715
00:43:28,139 --> 00:43:30,174
how can we throw out this meteorite?

716
00:43:30,241 --> 00:43:33,644
Then are you two just going to die
with the meteorite?

717
00:43:34,545 --> 00:43:36,214
Hey, Min-gi, Han-cheol.

718
00:43:36,280 --> 00:43:39,951
It breaks our hearts,
but let's let little Meteorite go.

719
00:43:50,128 --> 00:43:52,330
I can't!

720
00:43:52,396 --> 00:43:54,866
I can't do it. I can't either.

721
00:43:58,336 --> 00:43:59,670
Just toss it! Toss it!

722
00:43:59,737 --> 00:44:01,105
What's with you two?

723
00:44:01,172 --> 00:44:02,807
Fine, fine. I'll toss it.

724
00:44:02,874 --> 00:44:07,311
Let me at least say goodbye,
just one last goodbye.

725
00:44:07,912 --> 00:44:12,717
Meteorite, forgive me
for failing to protect you.

726
00:44:15,119 --> 00:44:19,023
Meteorite, may you go
to a better planet next time.

727
00:44:19,090 --> 00:44:20,858
Goodbye! Hey, toss it!

728
00:44:41,145 --> 00:44:44,048
What do I do? What do I do now?

729
00:44:47,051 --> 00:44:49,387
Meteorite…

730
00:44:50,188 --> 00:44:52,190
Thank you so much.

731
00:44:52,256 --> 00:44:54,058
Forget it, you silly girl.

732
00:44:54,125 --> 00:44:57,328
Stick with it this time
and really work hard, okay?

733
00:44:57,395 --> 00:44:59,797
Yes, I'll work really hard.

734
00:44:59,864 --> 00:45:01,499
Of course, you really should.

735
00:45:01,566 --> 00:45:03,768
Phew, that's a load off my mind.

736
00:45:03,834 --> 00:45:06,537
I can finally sleep easy tonight.

737
00:45:08,806 --> 00:45:11,242
What? Isn't that Mom over there?

738
00:45:11,309 --> 00:45:13,711
Isn't that Mr. Han next to her?

739
00:45:13,778 --> 00:45:15,813
Why are Mom and Mr. Han together?

740
00:45:15,880 --> 00:45:17,381
Can't you tell by looking?

741
00:45:17,448 --> 00:45:19,116
Oh, damn it!

742
00:45:19,183 --> 00:45:21,652
-Mom!

743
00:45:21,719 --> 00:45:23,054
Mom, what are you doing?

744
00:45:23,120 --> 00:45:24,655
What are you two up to?

745
00:45:24,722 --> 00:45:25,957
Oh, no. What do we do?

746
00:45:26,023 --> 00:45:27,825
What else can we do? Run!

747
00:45:28,726 --> 00:45:31,862
Mom, stop right there! Stop, Mom!

748
00:45:31,929 --> 00:45:33,965
Why are you running? Mom!

749
00:45:36,567 --> 00:45:40,204
Ma'am, I'm truly sorry.

750
00:45:40,271 --> 00:45:43,641
I'm well aware of how much I lack.

751
00:45:43,708 --> 00:45:46,510
I know I have no right to say this.

752
00:45:46,577 --> 00:45:50,681
But I really love… Sang-deuk.

753
00:45:51,549 --> 00:45:53,551
I love him with all my heart.

754
00:45:55,152 --> 00:45:56,954
I'll really do my very best.

755
00:45:57,021 --> 00:45:59,924
Please give us your blessing, okay?

756
00:46:07,431 --> 00:46:08,833
He's too good for you!

757
00:46:15,106 --> 00:46:16,874
Our poor little meteorite

758
00:46:16,941 --> 00:46:19,610
is down in that freezing water.

759
00:46:19,677 --> 00:46:21,512
How cold must it be?

760
00:46:21,579 --> 00:46:23,547
Knock it off, man.

761
00:46:24,115 --> 00:46:26,450
You keep reminding me of it.

762
00:46:27,451 --> 00:46:30,087
What do we do about our album?

763
00:46:30,154 --> 00:46:32,123
Honestly, we…

764
00:46:32,790 --> 00:46:35,493
I'm seriously going crazy.

765
00:46:35,559 --> 00:46:36,560
Oh, that's right!

766
00:46:36,627 --> 00:46:40,064
Sang-eun said she'd upload
our music video, remember?

767
00:46:40,131 --> 00:46:42,700
Should we just check the reaction?

768
00:46:42,767 --> 00:46:45,269
-Hurry, search it!
-I bet many people heard it.

769
00:46:45,336 --> 00:46:47,672
-Check the views.
-Probably about 3 million.

770
00:46:47,738 --> 00:46:49,006
VIEWS: 3

771
00:46:49,073 --> 00:46:50,341
Three? Three views?

772
00:46:50,408 --> 00:46:52,043
Three views?

773
00:46:52,810 --> 00:46:53,678
Three views?

774
00:46:53,744 --> 00:46:54,679
Three?

775
00:46:54,745 --> 00:46:57,348
I knew this would happen.

776
00:46:57,415 --> 00:46:59,417
It's all over for us now!

777
00:46:59,483 --> 00:47:01,252
It's really over!

778
00:47:04,255 --> 00:47:05,923
One, two, three.

779
00:47:08,726 --> 00:47:11,295
Yun-ha, uh… what brings you here?

780
00:47:11,362 --> 00:47:12,730
I have something to say.

781
00:47:12,797 --> 00:47:16,600
My company's CEO wants to see you all.

782
00:47:17,501 --> 00:47:19,503
-The CEO?
-Why would that jerk want us?

783
00:47:19,570 --> 00:47:23,574
He's planning a new band these days.

784
00:47:23,641 --> 00:47:27,211
I recommended you guys,
and he said he'd audition you.

785
00:47:28,379 --> 00:47:30,681
That jerk must really hate us.

786
00:47:30,748 --> 00:47:32,717
He says he's forgotten the past now.

787
00:47:32,783 --> 00:47:34,618
He hated seeing you go to waste.

788
00:47:35,753 --> 00:47:38,356
What do you say? Want to audition?

789
00:47:42,026 --> 00:47:45,229
Of course we'll do it! Uh… we will!

790
00:47:46,230 --> 00:47:48,532
Absolutely! Absolutely!
We absolutely must!

791
00:47:48,599 --> 00:47:51,469
Then I'll call to set up the audition.

792
00:47:51,535 --> 00:47:53,170
Thank you.

793
00:47:54,405 --> 00:47:56,040
Thank you!

794
00:47:57,308 --> 00:47:58,709
Jackpot! Our last chance!

795
00:47:58,776 --> 00:48:00,177
There's always a way out!

796
00:48:00,244 --> 00:48:01,479
Warm up your voice!

797
00:48:01,545 --> 00:48:03,280
Why warm up my voice now?

798
00:48:03,347 --> 00:48:04,982
Wait a second.

799
00:48:07,852 --> 00:48:10,187
-What?
-What are you scheming?

800
00:48:10,254 --> 00:48:11,889
What do you mean, scheming?

801
00:48:11,956 --> 00:48:15,426
The CEO wants to form a band,
so I just recommended you guys.

802
00:48:15,960 --> 00:48:17,862
Why? Can't I even do that?

803
00:48:17,928 --> 00:48:19,029
Is that really all?

804
00:48:19,096 --> 00:48:22,066
Yes. If we're done talking, can I go?

805
00:48:30,141 --> 00:48:34,078
Yes, I received all the materials
on the sixth industry.

806
00:48:34,145 --> 00:48:36,080
Yes, once the guys get back,

807
00:48:36,147 --> 00:48:38,449
I'll talk it over and call you back.

808
00:48:38,516 --> 00:48:41,519
Yes, thank you so much. Take care.

809
00:48:41,585 --> 00:48:43,220
Yes.

810
00:48:44,555 --> 00:48:46,357
SIXTH INDUSTRY STARTUP MANUAL

811
00:48:48,225 --> 00:48:50,361
We have to succeed no matter what.

812
00:48:50,428 --> 00:48:52,696
We have to sing "Memory," man.
"Memory."

813
00:48:52,763 --> 00:48:54,365
I told you, that song's iffy.

814
00:48:54,432 --> 00:48:56,333
Why are you guys so happy?

815
00:48:56,400 --> 00:48:57,268
Any good news?

816
00:48:57,334 --> 00:48:59,904
Yun-hui, we might release an album.

817
00:48:59,970 --> 00:49:01,372
We'll audition in Seoul.

818
00:49:01,439 --> 00:49:03,040
An audition?

819
00:49:03,107 --> 00:49:05,876
Yes, our former agency boss
is interested in us,

820
00:49:05,943 --> 00:49:08,379
and said to come up for an audition.

821
00:49:08,446 --> 00:49:11,315
If this audition goes well,
we could release an album

822
00:49:11,382 --> 00:49:13,184
even if we can't sell the cabbage.

823
00:49:13,250 --> 00:49:15,953
Really? That's so great!

824
00:49:16,020 --> 00:49:16,954
Congratulations!

825
00:49:17,021 --> 00:49:20,357
Oh, come on.
We haven't even auditioned yet.

826
00:49:21,358 --> 00:49:23,227
Hey, shouldn't we call Ki-jun?

827
00:49:23,294 --> 00:49:26,497
I did call him, but he didn't pick up.

828
00:49:27,398 --> 00:49:28,599
Let's try on our own.

829
00:49:28,666 --> 00:49:31,368
If it goes well, let's call him again.

830
00:49:31,435 --> 00:49:33,070
I'd hate to hurt him again.

831
00:49:33,137 --> 00:49:36,407
Okay, what the heck, let's go for it!

832
00:49:36,474 --> 00:49:38,576
Yun-hui, on that note, cook for us.

833
00:49:38,642 --> 00:49:40,911
We'll eat your food and practice hard.

834
00:49:40,978 --> 00:49:41,846
Gosh, alright.

835
00:49:41,912 --> 00:49:43,380
I'll make an amazing meal.

836
00:49:43,447 --> 00:49:45,182
-Just wait a bit.
-Got it.

837
00:49:45,249 --> 00:49:47,251
-Please grill us some beef.
-Alright.

838
00:49:47,318 --> 00:49:49,286
We have to do this one, "Memory."

839
00:49:55,226 --> 00:49:57,895
Gosh, I did all that work for nothing.

840
00:50:04,168 --> 00:50:06,971
Just when did you and In-ki
get together like that?

841
00:50:07,037 --> 00:50:08,939
It hasn't been long.

842
00:50:09,540 --> 00:50:11,075
You have quite the talent.

843
00:50:11,141 --> 00:50:14,044
You seduced a man 12 years
and a zodiac cycle younger.

844
00:50:14,111 --> 00:50:15,546
Is that so?

845
00:50:15,613 --> 00:50:18,215
My, is Mr. Han really that young?

846
00:50:18,282 --> 00:50:20,050
He looks a bit old for his age,

847
00:50:20,117 --> 00:50:21,452
and Botox pulls you taut

848
00:50:21,519 --> 00:50:23,687
so the age gap looks small, right?

849
00:50:23,754 --> 00:50:26,824
A whole zodiac cycle, a whole cycle!
Do you know that?

850
00:50:27,424 --> 00:50:30,027
Gosh, I'm too embarrassed
to face the village…

851
00:50:30,094 --> 00:50:33,230
What does age have to do with love?

852
00:50:33,297 --> 00:50:34,765
Mom!

853
00:50:34,832 --> 00:50:38,135
In-ki is only ten years older than me.

854
00:50:38,202 --> 00:50:39,303
Do you know that?

855
00:50:39,370 --> 00:50:42,239
Me calling him "Father"…

856
00:50:45,042 --> 00:50:47,111
This just isn't right, is it?

857
00:50:47,177 --> 00:50:50,014
Uh… who said we're getting married?

858
00:50:50,080 --> 00:50:51,649
You're making such a fuss.

859
00:50:51,715 --> 00:50:55,152
Anyway, I clearly told you no.

860
00:50:55,219 --> 00:50:57,755
Get over him and move on, okay?

861
00:51:11,235 --> 00:51:14,705
One, two, three, four.

862
00:51:29,653 --> 00:51:34,525
Though I spent another day without you

863
00:51:35,225 --> 00:51:38,028
Even if I cry out loud in sorrow

864
00:51:38,095 --> 00:51:42,132
Though you will never hear me

865
00:51:42,199 --> 00:51:45,369
Even today, it's only your name

866
00:51:45,436 --> 00:51:48,339
That I call out

867
00:51:51,408 --> 00:51:53,110
You guys are still good.

868
00:51:53,177 --> 00:51:56,213
Really? Thank you so much, sir!

869
00:51:56,280 --> 00:51:59,416
I've seen your skills, so just wait.

870
00:52:02,653 --> 00:52:05,689
Yes, thank you. Thank you, sir.

871
00:52:06,657 --> 00:52:11,061
Please give us a favorable decision.

872
00:52:11,128 --> 00:52:13,797
We will take our leave now, then.

873
00:52:13,864 --> 00:52:15,032
Thank you. Go on out.

874
00:52:15,099 --> 00:52:16,934
Thank you for your time, sir.

875
00:52:30,648 --> 00:52:34,284
It's me. The guys just came and went.

876
00:52:34,918 --> 00:52:37,287
I'll make their album like you asked.

877
00:52:37,354 --> 00:52:38,522
So hurry back now.

878
00:52:38,589 --> 00:52:40,290
All right.

879
00:52:40,357 --> 00:52:42,292
I'll return once I wrap things up.

880
00:52:42,359 --> 00:52:45,796
But this must stay a complete secret.

881
00:52:47,264 --> 00:52:48,932
I'll hang up now.

882
00:52:57,574 --> 00:53:02,012
I'm going crazy. Where on earth is it?

883
00:53:03,280 --> 00:53:05,549
That's what I'm saying.

884
00:53:05,616 --> 00:53:09,053
It'll be bad if someone else finds it.

885
00:53:09,119 --> 00:53:10,821
I know, right?

886
00:53:10,888 --> 00:53:15,325
It seems like more people keep coming.

887
00:53:16,126 --> 00:53:19,129
They say they're coming from all over.

888
00:53:19,196 --> 00:53:23,367
Why did that meteorite
have to fall here, darn it?

889
00:53:27,638 --> 00:53:29,907
HADUROK-RI

890
00:53:35,846 --> 00:53:37,548
HADUROK-RI

891
00:53:48,058 --> 00:53:49,393
What is that?

892
00:53:49,460 --> 00:53:51,495
I'm sure this is the right field.

893
00:53:51,562 --> 00:53:53,397
Who are all those people?

894
00:53:53,464 --> 00:53:55,899
I'm sure they'll leave soon.

895
00:53:57,367 --> 00:54:02,072
Now, where did I bury that container?

896
00:54:07,444 --> 00:54:10,314
That's right, there you are.

897
00:54:10,380 --> 00:54:12,449
The utility pole.

898
00:54:13,584 --> 00:54:18,355
It's exactly 50 steps
to the right of this pole.

899
00:54:19,089 --> 00:54:23,627
One, two, three, four, five.

900
00:54:24,995 --> 00:54:29,032
46, 47, 48.

901
00:54:30,200 --> 00:54:32,369
What's this?

902
00:54:35,205 --> 00:54:37,141
Aren't these cabbages?

903
00:54:37,207 --> 00:54:41,945
Jeez! Who piled these cabbages here?

904
00:54:46,116 --> 00:54:48,152
Argh!

905
00:54:48,218 --> 00:54:50,187
Cabbages!

906
00:54:50,254 --> 00:54:53,590
Seriously, these cabbages.

907
00:54:54,758 --> 00:54:57,795
This is driving me crazy.
What's with these cabbages?

908
00:54:57,861 --> 00:54:59,963
I'm losing my mind.

909
00:55:00,030 --> 00:55:02,232
Ow! Seriously!

910
00:55:02,299 --> 00:55:03,267
I'm sorry.

911
00:55:03,333 --> 00:55:04,902
Hey, watch where you're going!

912
00:55:04,968 --> 00:55:06,870
I… I'm sorry.

913
00:55:12,309 --> 00:55:14,878
Wait, it's you two.

914
00:55:14,945 --> 00:55:17,748
Why are you two here?

915
00:55:18,282 --> 00:55:22,152
Surely you're not here for my money?

916
00:55:22,219 --> 00:55:27,591
You tried to steal the money
while I was passed out, right?

917
00:55:28,192 --> 00:55:31,295
You thieving bitches! I'll teach you--

918
00:55:31,361 --> 00:55:32,462
Is that your money?

919
00:55:32,529 --> 00:55:34,631
You stole that money too, didn't you?

920
00:55:34,698 --> 00:55:37,801
You two have gone completely crazy.

921
00:55:37,868 --> 00:55:39,403
That's right, I'm crazy.

922
00:55:39,469 --> 00:55:41,305
Talk before the crazy bitch bites.

923
00:55:41,371 --> 00:55:43,307
Where's that money?

924
00:55:44,107 --> 00:55:45,809
Since you inquire so kindly…

925
00:55:45,876 --> 00:55:47,377
I have it right here, ma'am.

926
00:55:47,444 --> 00:55:49,346
Did you think I'd say that?

927
00:55:49,413 --> 00:55:52,850
Okay, so that's how you're playing it.

928
00:55:52,916 --> 00:55:56,220
If that assemblyman finds out,
he won't let this slide.

929
00:55:56,286 --> 00:55:57,721
-What?
-So just spill it.

930
00:55:57,788 --> 00:56:00,557
Before I call him and say you're here.

931
00:56:04,428 --> 00:56:05,495
We're back.

932
00:56:05,562 --> 00:56:07,698
Oh, you're back.

933
00:56:08,432 --> 00:56:10,100
Goodness.

934
00:56:12,202 --> 00:56:14,805
How was the audition? Did it go well?

935
00:56:14,872 --> 00:56:17,774
Well… it didn't just go well.

936
00:56:21,511 --> 00:56:24,081
We killed it! Yes!

937
00:56:24,147 --> 00:56:26,316
The CEO was totally blown away.

938
00:56:26,383 --> 00:56:28,952
Releasing an album now
is just a matter of time.

939
00:56:30,454 --> 00:56:31,755
Good work, guys.

940
00:56:31,822 --> 00:56:34,458
What a relief. I was so worried.

941
00:56:34,524 --> 00:56:37,127
Still, nothing is decided for sure yet.

942
00:56:37,194 --> 00:56:40,063
Even so, that's great! Congratulations!

943
00:56:40,130 --> 00:56:41,164
Thanks.

944
00:56:41,231 --> 00:56:44,968
So are you guys going to Seoul now?

945
00:56:45,636 --> 00:56:46,737
Yes, I guess so.

946
00:56:47,704 --> 00:56:50,307
Then I won't see you guys anymore.

947
00:56:56,046 --> 00:56:59,082
Don't be like that.
It's not like we'll never see you.

948
00:56:59,149 --> 00:57:01,051
We'll come visit you all the time.

949
00:57:01,118 --> 00:57:02,686
Right, that's right.

950
00:57:02,753 --> 00:57:04,688
We have good news! Why wait around?

951
00:57:04,755 --> 00:57:06,356
Let's throw a party! A party!

952
00:57:06,423 --> 00:57:08,225
No, no, no, please save the party

953
00:57:08,292 --> 00:57:11,194
until everything is decided.

954
00:57:11,261 --> 00:57:13,797
-Let me contact Ki-jun first.
-Okay.

955
00:57:13,864 --> 00:57:14,932
Have some fruit.

956
00:57:14,998 --> 00:57:16,800
Fruit, let's eat fruit, Yun-hui.

957
00:57:36,887 --> 00:57:38,622
What are you doing here?

958
00:57:40,557 --> 00:57:42,159
Nothing much.

959
00:57:43,226 --> 00:57:45,362
Did you get in touch with Ki-jun?

960
00:57:46,096 --> 00:57:46,997
Yes.

961
00:57:47,998 --> 00:57:49,733
But he says he won't do it.

962
00:57:50,434 --> 00:57:54,805
He says he's giving up music and drums.

963
00:57:55,806 --> 00:57:59,009
He's made up his mind,
so I hated to shake him up again…

964
00:58:03,246 --> 00:58:05,349
I feel awful, like it's all my fault.

965
00:58:05,415 --> 00:58:07,451
You did everything you could.

966
00:58:08,318 --> 00:58:10,554
And everyone makes their own choices.

967
00:58:10,620 --> 00:58:12,923
You don't need to worry about that.

968
00:58:15,158 --> 00:58:18,829
Anyway, you'll be heading to Seoul now.

969
00:58:19,529 --> 00:58:21,565
Must be nice.

970
00:58:21,631 --> 00:58:23,667
But I feel kind of strange.

971
00:58:24,668 --> 00:58:26,803
The cabbages are on my mind.

972
00:58:26,870 --> 00:58:29,239
So are the people in the village.

973
00:58:30,507 --> 00:58:32,142
I just feel unsettled.

974
00:58:34,044 --> 00:58:36,413
I'm worried about Min-ho.

975
00:58:36,480 --> 00:58:38,915
When you go to Seoul,
he'll miss you so much.

976
00:58:41,852 --> 00:58:43,420
What about you?

977
00:58:43,487 --> 00:58:47,924
Me? It'll be a huge relief for me.

978
00:58:47,991 --> 00:58:50,460
It'll feel like pulling a bad tooth.

979
00:58:50,527 --> 00:58:52,362
Really?

980
00:58:53,230 --> 00:58:55,432
I think I'm going to miss you.

981
00:58:56,566 --> 00:58:59,636
Who will I fight with without you now?

982
00:59:00,170 --> 00:59:03,040
And who'll put up with my bad temper?

983
00:59:03,840 --> 00:59:06,476
Only you ever put up with me.

984
00:59:06,543 --> 00:59:07,677
What do we do now?

985
00:59:09,112 --> 00:59:10,747
Come visit sometimes.

986
00:59:10,814 --> 00:59:13,517
I'll give you a really good fight.

987
00:59:15,485 --> 00:59:16,686
Okay.

988
00:59:23,593 --> 00:59:25,228
Gosh.

989
00:59:27,464 --> 00:59:30,100
So much has happened, right here.

990
00:59:33,236 --> 00:59:37,207
I thought you'd give up and leave,
but you held out for quite a while.

991
00:59:44,014 --> 00:59:45,415
Then there's our HyunA.

992
00:59:45,482 --> 00:59:47,117
HyunA kills it.

993
00:59:49,286 --> 00:59:51,788
She kills it. She's no joke.

994
00:59:51,855 --> 00:59:53,490
I mean, that--

995
00:59:53,557 --> 00:59:55,492
She's no joke, man.

996
01:00:07,170 --> 01:00:09,906
I'm studying, of course.

997
01:00:14,111 --> 01:00:15,779
What? An album?

998
01:00:21,251 --> 01:00:23,687
No… I'm going to sit this out.

999
01:00:25,355 --> 01:00:27,757
What? My dream?

1000
01:00:29,426 --> 01:00:31,061
Please, man…

1001
01:00:32,028 --> 01:00:35,165
A dream is just a dream.

1002
01:00:35,232 --> 01:00:37,534
I don't want
false hope torturing me again.

1003
01:00:46,143 --> 01:00:48,178
Ki-jun, congrats on your dorm return!

1004
01:00:48,245 --> 01:00:50,647
I'm so relieved you're back.

1005
01:00:50,714 --> 01:00:53,650
While you were gone,
I was dead last in our class.

1006
01:00:53,717 --> 01:00:55,585
I gladly return that spot to you.

1007
01:00:55,652 --> 01:00:57,220
Hahaha!

1008
01:00:57,287 --> 01:00:59,322
It feels like I escaped last place.

1009
01:00:59,389 --> 01:01:04,461
Karaoke for round two!
It's on me, on me, on me! Let's go!

1010
01:01:04,528 --> 01:01:05,629
Hey, get up!

1011
01:01:05,695 --> 01:01:07,597
-Get on up!
-Come on, get up!

1012
01:01:08,565 --> 01:01:12,669
Please look at me just once

1013
01:01:14,004 --> 01:01:17,541
Only you do not know

1014
01:01:17,607 --> 01:01:21,011
Only you do not hear

1015
01:01:21,077 --> 01:01:24,948
I call and call out, yet you don't…

1016
01:01:25,015 --> 01:01:26,449
Come on, let's go inside.

1017
01:01:26,516 --> 01:01:29,452
What are you,
some Joseon Dynasty noblewoman?

1018
01:01:29,519 --> 01:01:32,088
I just held your hand once, so what?
Get inside!

1019
01:01:33,924 --> 01:01:35,525
Release my hand.

1020
01:01:35,592 --> 01:01:37,360
Come on, get in here.

1021
01:01:41,865 --> 01:01:42,732
Release my hand.

1022
01:01:42,799 --> 01:01:45,368
Get in there! Hey, come here!

1023
01:01:46,503 --> 01:01:48,572
Yu-na.

1024
01:01:49,372 --> 01:01:51,007
Ki-jun.

1025
01:01:51,975 --> 01:01:55,178
What are you doing… here right now?

1026
01:01:56,046 --> 01:01:58,348
What is this?

1027
01:02:01,418 --> 01:02:03,520
You have no business ethics.

1028
01:02:03,587 --> 01:02:05,255
Get in here now.

1029
01:02:07,123 --> 01:02:09,292
What are you doing?

1030
01:02:09,359 --> 01:02:10,961
How dare you, little punk!

1031
01:02:11,027 --> 01:02:12,028
Get lost!

1032
01:02:12,095 --> 01:02:12,963
Get in here now.

1033
01:02:13,029 --> 01:02:15,465
What did you say, you son of a bitch?

1034
01:02:19,202 --> 01:02:20,904
Come with me.

1035
01:02:27,544 --> 01:02:29,512
Release me.

1036
01:02:30,180 --> 01:02:31,948
What on earth are you doing here?

1037
01:02:32,015 --> 01:02:33,750
I asked what you're doing!

1038
01:02:33,817 --> 01:02:36,319
I had to pay my mother's hospital bill.

1039
01:02:36,386 --> 01:02:37,754
I had no other choice.

1040
01:02:37,821 --> 01:02:40,590
So you do work like this?
Are you out of your mind?

1041
01:02:40,657 --> 01:02:42,959
I hate working
in a place like this too.

1042
01:02:43,026 --> 01:02:45,662
But I can only work
in a place like this.

1043
01:02:45,729 --> 01:02:46,896
What else can I do?

1044
01:02:48,198 --> 01:02:49,799
It breaks my heart too.

1045
01:02:50,667 --> 01:02:52,469
It hurts so much I could go crazy.

1046
01:03:01,278 --> 01:03:03,880
Hey! Who are you?

1047
01:03:04,681 --> 01:03:07,817
You get over here!
You punk, you're dead meat!

1048
01:03:07,884 --> 01:03:10,186
What, you bastard?
What did you just say?

1049
01:03:10,253 --> 01:03:11,755
Ki-jun, hold back. Stop.

1050
01:03:11,821 --> 01:03:12,956
You stay back!

1051
01:03:13,023 --> 01:03:15,892
-You crazy bastard!
-You punk, I'll beat you senseless!

1052
01:03:16,493 --> 01:03:18,795
You punk! You're done for today!

1053
01:03:18,862 --> 01:03:19,796
You're done for!

1054
01:03:19,863 --> 01:03:21,798
Stop this! Please stop this!

1055
01:03:21,865 --> 01:03:23,767
You're done for! Stupid woman!

1056
01:03:23,833 --> 01:03:25,602
You, get over here!

1057
01:03:25,669 --> 01:03:28,505
That bastard! I'll tear him apart!

1058
01:03:34,911 --> 01:03:36,680
Break it up, both of you. Stop.

1059
01:03:36,746 --> 01:03:38,415
Let go! I'll kill that bastard!

1060
01:03:38,481 --> 01:03:39,949
Come on, I said stop it.

1061
01:03:40,016 --> 01:03:42,485
That punk hit me like this first!

1062
01:03:42,552 --> 01:03:45,355
You two can explain it at the station.

1063
01:03:47,157 --> 01:03:49,326
Looks like you got hit too, miss.

1064
01:03:49,392 --> 01:03:50,994
How dare you hit a woman.

1065
01:03:51,061 --> 01:03:52,929
Are you all right?

1066
01:03:52,996 --> 01:03:55,298
Miss, please come with us for now.

1067
01:03:55,365 --> 01:03:58,735
It's no big deal.
You just need to give a statement.

1068
01:04:02,339 --> 01:04:03,773
What's wrong?

1069
01:04:03,840 --> 01:04:05,909
That's suspicious.

1070
01:04:05,975 --> 01:04:09,012
Miss, let me see your ID.

1071
01:04:12,082 --> 01:04:13,717
Your ID, please.

1072
01:04:18,421 --> 01:04:19,956
Hurry, go!

1073
01:04:29,866 --> 01:04:33,103
I gaze at you

1074
01:04:33,169 --> 01:04:36,373
I wait only for you

1075
01:04:36,439 --> 01:04:39,918
Always in the same place, the same…
